1	option	How did Lord Sinclair die?
2	line	Player	How did Lord Sinclair die?
2	line	Guard	Well, it's all very mysterious. Mary, the maid, found the body in the study next to his bedroom on the east wing of the ground floor.
2	line	Guard	The door was found locked from the inside, and he seemed to have been stabbed, but there was an odd smell in the room. Frankly, I'm stumped.
2	action	end
1	option	I know who did it!
2	line	Player	I know who did it!
2	line	Guard	Really? That was quick work! Who?
2	select	Select an Option
2	option	It was an intruder!
3	line	Player	It was an intruder!
3	line	Guard	That's what we were thinking too. That someone broke in to steal something, was discovered by Lord Sinclair, stabbed him and ran.
3	line	Guard	It's odd that apparently nothing was stolen though... Find out something has been stolen,
3	line	Guard	and the case is closed, but the murdered man was a friend of the King, and it's more than my job's worth not to investigate fully.
3	action	end
2	option	The butler did it!
3	line	Player	The butler did it!
3	line	Guard	I hope you have proof to that effect. We have to arrest someone for this and it seems to me that only the actual murderer would gain by falsely accusing someone.
3	line	Guard	Although having said that the butler is kind of shifty looking...
3	action	end
