0	section	Talking to Gossip
1	line	Player	I'm investigating the murder up at the Sinclair place.
1	line	Gossip	Murder is it? Well, I'm not really surprised...
1	select	Select an Option
1	option	What can you tell me about the Sinclairs?
2	line	Player	What can you tell me about the Sinclairs?
2	line	Gossip	Well, what do you want to know?
2	select	Select an Option
2	option	Tell me about Lord Sinclair.
3	line	Player	Tell me about Lord Sinclair.
3	line	Gossip	Old Lord Sinclair was a great man with a lot of respect in these parts. More than his worthless children have anyway.
3	line	Player	His children? They have something to gain by his death?
3	line	Gossip	Yes. You could say that. Not that I'm one to gossip.
3	action	end
2	option	Why do the Sinclairs live so far from town?
3	line	Player	Why do the Sinclairs live so far from town?
3	line	Gossip	Well, they used to live in the big castle, but old Lord Sinclair gave it up so that those strange knights could live there instead. So the king built him a new house to the North.
3	line	Gossip	It's more cramped than his old place, but he seemed to like it. His children were furious at him for doing it though!
3	action	end
2	option	What can you tell me about his sons?
3	line	Player	What can you tell me about his sons?
3	line	Gossip	His sons eh? They all have their own skeletons in their cupboards. You'll have to be more specific. Who are you interested in exactly?
3	select	Select an Option
3	option	Tell me about Bob.
4	line	Player	Tell me about Bob.
4	line	Gossip	Bob is an odd character indeed... I'm not one to gossip, but I heard Bob is addicted to Tea. He can't make
4	line	Gossip	it through the day without having at least 20 cups!
4	line	Gossip	You might not think that's such a big thing, but he has spent thousands of gold to feed his habit!
4	line	Gossip	At one point he stole a lot of silverware from the kitchen and pawned it just so he could afford to buy his daily tea allowance.
4	line	Gossip	If his father ever found out, he would be in so much trouble... he might even get disowned!
4	action	end
3	option	Tell me about David.
4	line	Player	Tell me about David.
4	line	Gossip	David... oh David... not many people know this, but David really has an anger problem. He's always screaming and shouting
4	line	Gossip	at the household servants when he's angry, and they live in a state of fear, always walking on eggshells around him, but none of them have the courage
4	line	Gossip	to talk to his father about his behaviour. If they did, Lord Sinclair would almost certainly
4	line	Gossip	kick him out of the house, as some of the servants have been there longer than he has, and he definitely has no right to treat them like he does... but I'm not one to gossip about people.
4	action	end
3	option	Tell me about Frank.
4	line	Player	Tell me about Frank.
4	line	Gossip	I'm not one to talk ill of people behind their back, but Frank is a real piece of work. He is an absolutely terrible gambler... he can't pass 2 dogs in the street without putting a bet on which one will bark first!
4	line	Gossip	He has already squandered all of his allowance, and I heard he had stolen a number of paintings of his fathers to sell to try and cover his debts, but he still owes a lot of
4	line	Gossip	people a lot of money. If his father ever found out, he would stop his income, and then he would be in serious trouble!
4	action	end
2	option	What can you tell me about his daughters?
3	line	Player	What can you tell me about his daughters?
3	line	Gossip	His daughters eh? They're all nasty pieces of work. which of them specifically did you want to know about?
3	select	Select an Option
3	option	Tell me about Anna.
4	line	Player	Tell me about Anna.
4	line	Gossip	Anna... ah yes... Anna has 2 great loves:
4	line	Gossip	Sewing and gardening. But one thing she has kept secret is that she once had an affair with Stanford the gardener, and tried to get him fired when they broke up,
4	line	Gossip	by killing all of the flowers in the garden. If her father ever found out she had done that he would be so furious he would probably disown her.
4	action	end
3	option	Tell me about Carol.
4	line	Player	Tell me about Carol.
4	line	Gossip	Oh Carol... she is such a fool. You didn't hear this from me, but I heard a while ago she was conned out of a lot of money by a travelling salesman who sold her a box full
4	line	Gossip	of beans by telling her they were magic. But they weren't. She sold some rare books from the library to cover her debts, but
4	line	Gossip	her father would be incredibly annoyed if he ever found out - he might even throw her out of the house!
4	action	end
3	option	Tell me about Elizabeth.
4	line	Player	Tell me about Elizabeth.
4	line	Gossip	Elizabeth? Elizabeth has a strange problem... She cannot help herself, but is always stealing small objects - it's pretty sad that she is rich enough to afford to buy things, but would rather steal them instead.
4	line	Gossip	Now, I don't want to spread stories, but I heard she even stole a silver needle from her father that had great sentimental value for him.
4	line	Gossip	He was devastated when it was lost, and cried for a week thinking he had lost it!
4	line	Gossip	If he ever found out that it was her who had stolen it he would go absolutely mental, maybe even disowning her!
4	action	end
1	option	Who do you think was responsible?
2	line	Player	Who do you think was responsible?
2	line	Gossip	Well, I guess it could have been an intruder, but with that big guard dog of theirs I seriously doubt it. I suspect it was someone closer to home...
2	line	Gossip	Especially as I heard that the poison salesman in the Seers' village made a big sale to one of the family the other day.
2	action	end
1	option	I think the butler did it.
2	line	Player	I think the butler did it.
2	line	Gossip	And I think you've been reading too many cheap detective novels. Hobbes is kind of uptight, but his loyalty to old Lord Sinclair is beyond question.
2	action	end
1	option	I am so confused about who did it.
2	line	Player	I am so confused about who did it...
2	line	Player	Think you could give me any hints?
2	line	Gossip	Well, I don't know if it's related, but I heard from that Poison Salesman in town that he sold some poison to one of the Sinclair family
2	line	Gossip	the other day. I don't think he has any stock left now though...
2	action	end
