0	section	Talking to the Guard with all evidence
1	select	Select an Option
1	option	What should I be doing to help again?
2	action	above
1	option	How did Lord Sinclair die?
2	action	above
1	option	I know who did it!
2	line	Player	I know who did it!
2	line	Player	I have conclusive proof who the killer was.
2	line	Guard	You do? That's excellent work. Let's hear it then.
2	line	Player	I don't think it was an intruder, and I don't think Lord Sinclair was killed by being stabbed.
2	line	Guard	Hmmm? Really? Why not?
2	line	Player	Nobody heard the guard dog barking, which it would have if it had been an intruder who was responsible.
2	line	Player	Nobody heard any signs of a struggle either. I think the knife was there to throw suspicion away from the real culprit.
2	line	Guard	Yes, that makes sense. But who did do it then?
2	cond	If Anna is the murderer:
3	box	You prove to the guard the thread matches Anna's clothes.
3	line	Guard	Yes, I'd have to agree with that... but we need more evidence!
3	box	You prove to the guard Anna did not use poison on the compost heap.
3	line	Guard	Excellent work - have you considered a career as a detective? But I'm afraid it's still not quite enough...
3	box	You match Anna's finger prints with those on the dagger found in the body of Lord Sinclair.
3	line	Guard	Yes. There's no doubt about it. It must have been Anna who killed her father. All of the guards must congratulate you on your excellent work in helping us to solve this case.
